"""
=========================================================================================
AURA :: HYENA V11.2 STATEFUL LM ENGINE
=========================================================================================
CLI (v12.1): no options -> pygame GUI (default). --console -> interactive console
GUI (menu covering every feature). --help -> all flags + examples with defaults read
live from settings.json. Headless actions: --train / --finetune / --load-checkpoint /
--generate / --chat / --convert-gguf / --api, plus a --kebab-case override for every
settings.json field (e.g. --epochs 50 --learning-rate 1e-3 --no-grad-checkpoint).
Built on the v10 core (Hyena conv + fused-QKV causal attention feeding the gate,
O(1) stateful stepping, GGUF->Aura SVD transplant, EWC, JSON settings w/ live sync).

V12.1 GGUF CONVERSION OVERHAUL (garbled-output root-cause fixes):
  - GGUF-native unigram tokenizer (GGUFUnigramCodec): Viterbi segmentation over
    the file's own 262k vocab; token IDs round-trip 1:1 with the source model.
    The old path interpolated embeddings onto the tiktoken vocab -> garbled text.
  - Auto-sizing: d_model / n_layers / n_heads are read from GGUF metadata
    (general.architecture.*) and override the settings values, so you no longer
    need to guess "how large the model needs to be" for a conversion.
  - Gemma RMSNorm offset: gemma stores norm weights as (scale - 1); +1.0 is
    added back during transplant (raw copy zeroed the signal -> noise output).
  - Real attention transplant: Q/K/V are fused into c_attn (previously random),
    Wo -> c_proj + gate; gated-MLP gate_proj -> ffn[0], down_proj -> ffn[2].
  - RoPE theta from metadata (gemma3: local 1e4, every 6th layer global 1e6)
    via per-layer rope_base; new settings: rope_base / rope_global_every /
    rope_global_base.
  - The tokenizer travels inside the checkpoint ("gguf_tokenizer" blob), so
    loading a converted model always decodes with the right vocab; generation
    stops on <eos>/<end_of_turn> for instruct models.

V11.2 FIXES / IMPROVEMENTS (on top of V11.1):
  - CRITICAL: short-sequence / large-kernel crash fixed. When prefill T < kernel_size-1
    the extracted conv state was undersized; left-pad to full (k-1) + defensive pad in
    _causal_conv_step so "Kernel size can't be greater than actual input size" never
    fires again (the error you saw with kernel=64 and short prompts).
  - Chat panel now has its own cyan draggable ScrollThumb (non-overlapping with bubbles).
  - Auto-clear CUDA cache + gc on Stop training.
  - Load checkpoint allowed at any time: auto-stops the current run cleanly first.
  - Full hyper-param stamp (train_dtype incl. q4/q8, encoding, n_heads, etc.) written
    into every checkpoint; on load the live settings widgets are refreshed. Missing
    keys from older checkpoints fall back to current defaults (backwards-compatible).
  - Streaming token output: tokens appear in the chat bubble live as they are generated.
  - torch.cuda.amp.autocast -> torch.amp.autocast('cuda', ...) (silences the FutureWarning).
  - meta_generate: multi-suffix lookup + opportunistic verified ground-truth span commits
    so the cache is actually useful outside pure Erdos-Straus data.
  - Larger default window (1680x1020), title/stats no longer overlap at the top bar,
    tighter layout margins, no text can escape panel bounds.
  - n_heads remains fully variable at build/load time (settings value is the target;
    weights are adapted). Cannot hot-swap mid-training (tensor shapes are fixed at
    construction) -- this is documented in the load log.

V11.1 FIXES (retained):
  - ChatPanel per-turn layout cache.
  - Robust tiktoken decode that silently skips unassigned gap token IDs.
  - Settings save: retry + chmod + direct-write fallback for Windows WinError 5.
  - Real LR schedule: linear warmup then cosine decay to min_lr.
  - EWC Fisher/anchor device cache.
  - is_busy / race guards; MetaScratchpad returns Future + has shutdown().

WHAT'S NEW IN V11 (honest descriptions retained):
1) Generation-slowdown fix (KV/prefill hard-capped to block_size).
2) aurora_astralis verbatim cache (dictionary lookup of verified spans only).
3) meta_scratchpad (real CPU+GPU concurrent offload of non-CUDA work).
4) Full GUI + remaining features as previously specified.
=========================================================================================
"""

